# sha256 of every prebuilt Nim toolchain archive served from
# https://archive.frameos.net/prebuilt-deps/<target>/nim-<version>.tar.gz.
#
# The CDN is a plain R2 bucket: whoever can write to it (or sit between it and
# a runner) can hand CI a compiler. Every consumer looks its target up here
# and refuses to extract an archive whose digest is not on this list:
#   - Dockerfile, stage `nim-toolchain` (docker-publish-multi.yml,
#     e2e-docker.yml and any local `docker build`)
#   - .github/workflows/docker-publish-multi.yml, "Install Nim (prebuilt)"
#   - .github/workflows/frameos-cross.yml, "Install Nim (prebuilt)" (x2)
# A target with no line here fails the build; do not make that conditional.
# tools/prebuilt-deps/manifest.json is NOT the pin: r2_sync.py rewrites it
# from a fixed schema and mirrors it to the same bucket.
#
# Update recipe (after `tools/prebuilt-deps/r2_sync.py upload` of a new Nim):
#   1. bump the version in the paths below (sed -i 's/nim-2.2.4/nim-X.Y.Z/')
#   2. from a scratch dir, re-download exactly the paths this file lists and
#      paste the output over the entries:
#        grep -v '^#' /path/to/nim-prebuilt.sha256 | awk '{print $2}' |
#          while read -r p; do mkdir -p "${p%/*}" &&
#            curl -fsSL "https://archive.frameos.net/prebuilt-deps/$p" -o "$p"; done
#        sha256sum */nim-*.tar.gz
#   3. `sha256sum -c` the file against that scratch dir before committing.
# Targets that ship quickjs only (debian-*-armv6) have no Nim archive and are
# deliberately absent; ubuntu-*-armhf is accepted by the Dockerfile's case
# list but has never been published, so it is absent too.
#
# Format: `sha256sum -c` lines, keyed by `<target>/nim-<version>.tar.gz`.
